index 0000000..b77bd0b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SOLUTION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Solution
+
+Two bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`:
+
+1. **`get` did not refresh recency.** The docstring promises that both `get`
+   and `put` count as a "use", but `get` returned the value without moving the
+   key to the most-recently-used end of the `OrderedDict`. As a result a
+   recently-read key could be wrongly evicted as if it were the least recently
+   used. Fixed by calling `self._data.move_to_end(key)` on a successful `get`.
+
+2. **`put` evicted an entry when updating an existing key.** The eviction check
+   (`len(self._data) >= self.capacity`) ran unconditionally, so re-putting a key
+   that was already present at full capacity would pop an innocent
+   least-recently-used entry even though the total count wasn't growing. Fixed
+   by only evicting when the key is new (`key not in self._data`).
